    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0665" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.001 Vargas, Getulio/134: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-06T17:00:00-03:00">January 6, 1943—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. For the Under Secretary. Aranha<anchor n="93" xml:id="d601-f1"/> tells me
                        Martins<anchor n="94" xml:id="d601-f2"/> reports President Roosevelt told
                    him to invite President Vargas “to meet him at Trinidad” (when, not known).</p>
                <p>President Vargas says he will be glad to do it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d601-f1" n="93" xml:id="d601-f1-content">
                <p>Oswaldo Aranha, Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d601-f2" n="94" xml:id="d601-f2-content">
                <p>Carlos Martins, Brazilian Ambassador in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
